{"author":{"id":"15a88cc68503e42ab24006333304090e606ec65782bc59288f3c1c3e49bb4654"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785754437,"nonce":"GWTd9TWkA6C9TG9p+xJ8I2J3g/w=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOOEv6_s8AAAABLPGvew","github-url":"https://github.com/graphcore-research/gwr/issues/319","origin":"github"},"title":"Create generic compute support in gwr-timetable","message":"We should have support for a generic compute nodes in the timetable graph. It should support N inputs and M outputs and allow the user to define the number of machine operations that it will consume. Then we can evaluate graphs with other operations without having to write them all in GWR.\n\nThe downside will be that we won't be able to put them into the generator as easily as they won't be able to derive inputs/outputs for forward/backward graph generation. It will be possible, but they could be random and not necessarily sensible.\n\nThis would allow us to describe custom operators that do not yet exist and we should be able to target this from our ONNX to timetable translation tool.","files":null}]}